  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Restore full UK sovereignty by repealing the European Communities Act, keep the pound, and defend common-law liberties while re-enacting the Human Rights Act to align with British tradition; strengthen Parliament and a robust Lords, and root citizenship in British history. Invest in care via NHS +£2bn, nurses’ pay +£0.5bn, pensions +£5/week, elderly care funding, 30,000 more teachers, and 25,000 more police with deterrent sentencing and rehabilitation. Advance proportionality through tax simplification, raising the income-tax threshold to lift low earners out of tax, deregulation prioritising small firms, and skills-based immigration. TEXT_G: Prioritise Scottish independence and more powers from Westminster, a new written constitution, removal of Trident, and phased withdrawal from NATO’s nuclear structures. Expand care/equality with free personal care for all elderly, more nurses, free dental check-ups, prescription charge freeze, anti-poverty and homelessness measures, higher minimum wage, union rights, and stronger equality/disability rights. Add authority elements with 1,000 more police, tougher action on drug dealers, parental compensation orders, and lifelong restrictions for high-risk sex offenders.",
  "reasoning": "Because care and authority are the electorate’s top priorities, TEXT_C pairs significant care spending with a strong affirmation of British legal/constitutional authority and tradition, while also signalling proportionality through tax and regulatory reforms. TEXT_G emphasizes care and equality but centers Scottish independence and challenges existing UK/NATO authority, which is less aligned with the electorate’s authority priority and provides weaker proportionality cues.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_C"
}
